course: dictionary
lesson: 14964
title: Relocated: moved to a new place
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Relocated» is a slightly formal word for «moved». It means moved to a new place to live or work. «The family relocated to Leeds for Dad's new job.» They moved house to a new city, so relocated means moved to live somewhere else.
explain: The word can also describe things, not just people. «The company relocated its office to the other side of the city.» An office is not alive, but it can still be moved to a new place. Animals can be relocated too, for example to a safer home.
explain: Look for clues around the word. Job, office, safer and new place all tell you that a move has happened. Try the swap test: put «moved» in place of «relocated». «The family moved to Leeds for Dad's new job» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Relocated is the past tense of relocate. Relocate, relocates and relocating are other forms of the same word. «The owls were relocated last spring» means someone moved them to a new place, and it has already happened.
fact: Relocate is a verb, so it describes an action.
fact: «Relocated» means moved to a new place to live or work, or moved something, such as an office or an animal, to a new place.
fact: «Relocated» is a formal word for «moved». You will often see it in writing, but in talking you can usually say «moved».
fact: Common phrases are relocated to and was relocated, as in «The shop was relocated to the High Street.»
fact: Relocated can also be an adjective, as in «the relocated family», meaning a family that has moved to a new place.
exercise: «The family relocated to a city by the sea for Mum's new job.» What does relocated mean here? | Stayed at home all year | Lost their way on holiday | *Moved to a new place to live | Cleaned the house from top to bottom
exercise: «The school library was relocated to the top floor while the old room was repaired.» Find and copy one word that means moved. | floor | repaired | *relocated | library
exercise: «Wildlife workers relocated the squirrels to a safer wood.» Why might workers relocate animals? | *To move them to a safer home | To make them lose their homes | To count how many legs they have | To teach them to fly
test: «The company relocated its offices after the flood damaged the old building.» What does relocated mean? | Opened late | Closed for ever | Ruined | *Moved to a new place
test: Which word is a more formal way to say «moved»? | *relocated | drooped | glowed | crumbled
exam: «After the storm, the owl was relocated to a quiet forest.» Why was the owl relocated? | Because it was sleeping in the wrong place | *Because its old home was no longer safe | Because the forest had lost all its trees | Because it wanted a new name
